<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bhagalpur</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bhagalpur is a city in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bihar">Bihar</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, on the southern bank of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ganges-plain">Ganges</a>. Nearby lay <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/champa">Champa</a>, capital of the ancient kingdom of Anga, and in its district are the ruins of the Buddhist monastic university of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikramashila">Vikramashila</a>, founded under the Pala dynasty. Bhagalpur has long been known for its tussar <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silk">silk</a> weaving and is the centre of a district and division of the same name.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bhagalpur.jpg" alt="Bhagalpur" width="320" height="335" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jahaj · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ghantaghar_Bhagalpur.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
